# oracle: eFF H2 (128 electrons and nuclei, periodic) pair eff/cut with pressure/evirials under fix nve/eff: 4 steps, write_restart, clear, read_restart (no pair_style or pair_coeff, fix and compute re-specified), 4 more steps; electron spin, eradius and ervel come back from the file (pair_eff.rst: "These pair styles write their information to binary restart files"; examples/PACKAGES/eff/Li-dendritic restart path)
# oracle-inputs: w63eff_h2.data
# oracle-files: w174mx_eff_restart_er.dump
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-7 abs=1e-9 filerel=1e-7
units           electron
newton          on
boundary        p p p
atom_style      electron
read_data       w63eff_h2.data
pair_style      eff/cut 6.447968 pressure/evirials
pair_coeff      * *
comm_modify     vel yes
compute         effTemp all temp/eff
thermo          2
thermo_style    custom step etotal pe ke temp
thermo_modify   temp effTemp format float %.15g
timestep        0.0005
velocity        all create 300.0 4928459 dist gaussian rot yes mom yes
compute         er all property/atom spin eradius ervel erforce
fix             1 all nve/eff
run             4
write_restart   w174mx_eff.restart
clear
read_restart    w174mx_eff.restart
compute         effTemp all temp/eff
compute         er all property/atom spin eradius ervel erforce
thermo          2
thermo_style    custom step etotal pe ke temp
thermo_modify   temp effTemp format float %.15g
fix             1 all nve/eff
run             4
write_dump      all custom w174mx_eff_restart_er.dump id c_er[1] c_er[2] c_er[3] c_er[4] modify format float %.15g
